# Secrets for dev scripts (logo fetching, etc.)
# Copy to .env.scripts (gitignored) at the repo root and fill in values.
# Scripts that need these read directly from the repo root.
#
# This file is the convenience path for maintainers working in a checkout.
# Operators should pass these as ordinary environment variables instead —
# process.env takes precedence over this file. See
# docs/operations/platform-logos.md.

# ── Brandfetch Logo API ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OpenSteward ships no platform logos: Brandfetch's terms prohibit caching
# their CDN without an agreement, and the logos are 1,474 other companies'
# trademarks. Operators opt in via LOGO_SOURCE (none|cdn|local).
#
# This ID is needed to populate LOGO_SOURCE=local:
#
#   BRANDFETCH_CLIENT_ID=<id> pnpm --filter integration-server fetch:logos
#
# It is also what LOGO_SOURCE=cdn embeds in the page. Not a secret —
# Brandfetch designed it to be embedded in public <img> tags — but it is
# rate-limited per customer, so treat it as yours.
#
# Get a client ID at: https://brandfetch.com/developers
BRANDFETCH_CLIENT_ID=your-brandfetch-client-id

# Optional. Sent as the `Referer` header on Brandfetch CDN requests. Should
# match the origin registered for your Brandfetch app. Defaults to
# https://github.com/open-steward/opensteward if unset.
# BRANDFETCH_REFERER=https://your-org.example.com
